📘 Madhuram – ITR (Installation Test Report) API Documentation
Overview
The ITR API helps Madhuram track Installation Test Reports (WIR) once work is inspected.
It supports fetching lists, creating new ITRs, updating existing records, and deleting entries.
Authentication via JWT is required for all endpoints (Authorization: Bearer <token>).

Base URL: https://api.festmate.in

✅ ITR Object Highlights
- itr_id / id (integer) – unique record identifier
- itr_ref_no (string) – generated ITR number (e.g., ITR-SIGNET-1-ME-PR-PL-047)
- project_name, project_code, client_name (strings)
- contractor, pmc_engineer, vendor_code, material_code (strings)
- wir_itr_submission_date_time, inspection_date_time (datetime strings)
- submitted_to/submitted_by (strings)
- contractor_part (object) – nested details (location, area, discipline, attachments, measurement, clearances, comments, readiness)
- lodha_pmc (object) – PMC comments, sign-offs, result code
- source, source_file_name (strings) – extraction source metadata
- dynamic_field (array) – arbitrary key/value metadata for future compatibility
- project_id (integer) – reference to linked project
- status / itr_submitted (string/boolean) – workflow state (Draft/Submitted)

Endpoints
1️⃣ Create ITR
- `POST /api/itr`
- Body: JSON
  * Include header/project metadata plus `contractor_part`, `lodha_pmc`, and `dynamic_field`.
  * `project_id` is required (FK) so provide a valid project.
  * Example payload (subset):
```
{
  "project_name": "Signet Tower 1",
  "project_code": "SIGNET-1",
  "contractor": "Madhuram Enterprises",
  "itr_ref_no": "ITR-SIGNET-1-ME-PR-PL-047",
  "inspection_date_time": "2026-02-02T10:00:00Z",
  "contractor_part": {
    "location_ref": "Signet 1 - Plumbing",
    "description_of_works": "Pipe installation",
    "discipline": ["Plumbing"],
    "measurement": { "previous_qty": 0, "current_qty": 17, "cumulative_qty": 17 }
  },
  "project_id": 5
}
```
2️⃣ List ITRs
- `GET /api/itr`
- Returns array of all ITR records (latest first).

3️⃣ Get ITR by ID
- `GET /api/itr/{id}`
- Fetches a single ITR row by its `itr_id`.

4️⃣ Get ITR by Project
- `GET /api/itr/project/{projectId}`
- Lists ITRs scoped to a specific project (use the project’s `project_id`).

5️⃣ Update ITR
- `PUT /api/itr/{id}`
- Accepts partial payload; only provided fields are overwritten.
- Example updates: `lodha_pmc.result_code`, `contractor_part.description_of_works`, `itr_submitted`

6️⃣ Delete ITR
- `DELETE /api/itr/{id}`
- Removes the record; ensure no dependent workflows require the item afterwards.

Untracked Notes
- API responses mirror the payload (camelCase in frontend, snake_case in backend). The client helpers normalize between both formats.
